scheduler: pass LD_LIBRARY_PATH to filters and backends on QNX

cupsd, running as root, gives its filters, backends and helper programs a
clean environment and refuses to pass on any LD_ variable. On QNX the
libraries of anything installed outside the system directories (libcups
itself under /usr/local/lib, and on a minimal image QNX's own
libeventfd/libsocket companions in a separate directory) are only found
through LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so no filter could start ("Could not load library
libcups.so.2"). Pass LD_LIBRARY_PATH -- the one cupsd itself was started
with -- on QNX; LD_PRELOAD and the other loader variables stay blocked.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/scheduler/env.c
+++ b/scheduler/env.c
@@ -120,8 +120,21 @@
   */
 
 #if !CUPS_SNAP
+#  ifdef __QNX__
+ /*
+  * QNX: libraries installed outside the system's own directories (under
+  * /usr/local, say) are only found through LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so the search
+  * path cupsd was started with is passed on to its filters and backends;
+  * the other LD_ variables (LD_PRELOAD ...) are still not.
+  */
+
+  if (!RunUser && strcmp(name, "LD_LIBRARY_PATH") &&
+      (!strncmp(name, "DYLD_", 5) || !strncmp(name, "LD_", 3)))
+    return;
+#  else
   if (!RunUser && (!strncmp(name, "DYLD_", 5) || !strncmp(name, "LD_", 3)))
     return;
+#  endif /* __QNX__ */
 #endif /* !CUPS_SNAP */
 
  /*
